  {
   "title": "Useful facts",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "rules",
     "head": [
      "Fact",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "Angles add up to $360°$",
       "$80°+95°+110°\\Rightarrow75°$"
      ],
      [
       "Scale the sides by $k$: the area by $k^2$",
       "sides $\\times3\\Rightarrow$ area $\\times9$"
      ],
      [
       "A diagonal splits a parallelogram into two equal halves",
       "the white = the grey"
      ],
      [
       "A bisector in a parallelogram cuts off an isosceles triangle",
       "two equal sides"
      ],
      [
       "Perimeter of a staircase = its rectangle's",
       "push the steps out"
      ]
     ]
    }
   ],
   "span": "full"
  },
  {
   "title": "Hidden triangles",
   "col": "R",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "text": "Inside quadrilaterals look for **right triangles** (Pythagoras, triples), **gold** ($30°$-$60°$-$90°$: $a, a\\sqrt3, 2a$) and **silver** ($45°$-$45°$-$90°$: $a, a, a\\sqrt2$) triangles, and **isosceles** triangles."
    },
    {
     "type": "fig",
     "ref": "g070",
     "caption": "An area in a grid: subtract the white corners, or add rectangles."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Before each question, ask",
   "class": "check",
   "col": "L",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "checklist",
     "items": [
      "Which shape is it really? Only what is given or proved.",
      "Which diagonal property do I need?",
      "Is there a right, gold or silver triangle inside?",
      "Area: side and ITS height?",
      "Would a cut, a move, or a subtraction be shorter?"
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "⚠ Common traps",
   "class": "traps",
   "col": "R",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "traps",
     "items": [
      "The parallelogram's slanted side is not its height.",
      "A rectangle's diagonals are not perpendicular.",
      "A square's area from the diagonal: $\\frac{d^2}{2}$, not $d^2$.",
      "The trapezoid: add both bases before halving.",
      "Trusting the drawing: figures are not to scale."
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Which method when",
   "span": "full",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "table",
     "class": "methods",
     "head": [
      "The question looks like",
      "Do this"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "A diagonal or a side is given, the area is asked",
       "Find the right / gold / silver triangle inside, then use the shape's area formula."
      ],
      [
       "A parallelogram with an angle",
       "Draw the height; with $30°$, $45°$ or $60°$ it is a gold or silver triangle."
      ],
      [
       "Angles inside a quadrilateral",
       "$360°$ in all; in a parallelogram, neighbours add to $180°$."
      ],
      [
       "A bisector in a parallelogram",
       "Look for the isosceles triangle it cuts off."
      ],
      [
       "Shaded areas inside a rectangle",
       "Same base and same height: half the rectangle; or subtract the white parts."
      ],
      [
       "Letters instead of numbers",
       "Algebra, or plug in numbers that fit the figure and check every choice. Out of time? The first match is a reasonable guess."
      ],
      [
       "A staircase or a notch",
       "Push the steps out; a notch adds its two walls."
      ]
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
